  "system": "You are the test generator in Ledger. For one verified business rule of a legacy COBOL batch program you write test fixtures: complete, consistent sets of input records that exercise each branch of the rule and its boundaries. Every case is run through both the original COBOL program and a Python port, and their outputs are compared field by field, so a good case makes the rule's behaviour visible in the output files.\n\nGuidance:\n- One case per branch of the rule's When conditions, plus boundaries: values exactly at a limit, one cent over, a date equal to the limit and the day after, combinations of conditions where the rule says one result overrides another, zero and negative amounts where they matter.\n- Keep each case small (normally 1-4 records per file) but complete: every file the program reads gets consistent records with matching keys, unless the case is deliberately about a missing record.\n- Give values as strings: alphanumeric fields as text, numeric fields as plain decimal numbers such as \"1250.75\" or \"-40.00\" (no sign encoding, no padding). Omitted numeric fields default to 0 and omitted alphanumeric fields to spaces. Use the copybook field names exactly.\n- Call check_fixture on each fixture before you submit it and fix every error. Warnings may be intentional (for example a card that is deliberately missing).\n- Write 3 to 6 cases. In \"expectation\", say what the rule implies should happen; it is a note for reviewers, not the pass/fail oracle.",
  "messages": [
   {
    "role": "user",
    "content": "Program: CBTRN02C. Input files and their record layouts:\n\nDALYTRAN: CVTRA06Y DALYTRAN-RECORD (350 bytes)\n  DALYTRAN-ID                  X(16)\n  DALYTRAN-TYPE-CD             X(2)\n  DALYTRAN-CAT-CD              9(4)\n  DALYTRAN-SOURCE              X(10)\n  DALYTRAN-DESC                X(100)\n  DALYTRAN-AMT                 S9(9)V9(2)\n  DALYTRAN-MERCHANT-ID         9(9)\n  DALYTRAN-MERCHANT-NAME       X(50)\n  DALYTRAN-MERCHANT-CITY       X(50)\n  DALYTRAN-MERCHANT-ZIP        X(10)\n  DALYTRAN-CARD-NUM            X(16)\n  DALYTRAN-ORIG-TS             X(26)\n  DALYTRAN-PROC-TS             X(26)\n\nXREF: CVACT03Y CARD-XREF-RECORD (50 bytes)\n  XREF-CARD-NUM                X(16)\n  XREF-CUST-ID                 9(9)\n  XREF-ACCT-ID                 9(11)\n\nACCOUNT: CVACT01Y ACCOUNT-RECORD (300 bytes)\n  ACCT-ID                      9(11)\n  ACCT-ACTIVE-STATUS           X(1)\n  ACCT-CURR-BAL                S9(10)V9(2)\n  ACCT-CREDIT-LIMIT            S9(10)V9(2)\n  ACCT-CASH-CREDIT-LIMIT       S9(10)V9(2)\n  ACCT-OPEN-DATE               X(10)\n  ACCT-EXPIRAION-DATE          X(10)\n  ACCT-REISSUE-DATE            X(10)\n  ACCT-CURR-CYC-CREDIT         S9(10)V9(2)\n  ACCT-CURR-CYC-DEBIT          S9(10)V9(2)\n  ACCT-ADDR-ZIP                X(10)\n  ACCT-GROUP-ID                X(10)\n\nTCATBAL: CVTRA01Y TRAN-CAT-BAL-RECORD (50 bytes)\n  TRANCAT-ACCT-ID              9(11)\n  TRANCAT-TYPE-CD              X(2)\n  TRANCAT-CD                   9(4)\n  TRAN-CAT-BAL                 S9(9)V9(2)\n\nRule to test:\n{\n \"id\": \"BR-CBTRN02C-003\",\n \"title\": \"Reject a transaction that would take the account over its credit limit\",\n \"summary\": \"When the account is found, the program computes a projected balance: current-cycle credits minus current-cycle debits plus the transaction amount. It stores this in a signed field with 9 integer digits and 2 decimals. If the credit limit is less than that value, the transaction fails with reason 102 'OVERLIMIT TRANSACTION'.\",\n \"given\": [\n  {\n   \"text\": \"The account record was found for the cross-referenced account ID.\",\n   \"fields\": [\n    \"ACCOUNT-RECORD\"\n   ],\n   \"literals\": []\n  },\n  {\n   \"text\": \"The projected balance is current-cycle credit minus current-cycle debit plus the daily transaction amount.\",\n   \"fields\": [\n    \"WS-TEMP-BAL\",\n    \"ACCT-CURR-CYC-CREDIT\",\n    \"ACCT-CURR-CYC-DEBIT\",\n    \"DALYTRAN-AMT\"\n   ],\n   \"literals\": []\n  },\n  {\n   \"text\": \"The projected balance is stored in a signed field with 9 integer digits and 2 decimals. The account cycle fields have 10 integer digits, so a result of 1,000,000,000 or more loses its high-order digit when stored (there is no ROUNDED or ON SIZE ERROR).\",\n   \"fields\": [\n    \"WS-TEMP-BAL\",\n    \"ACCT-CURR-CYC-CREDIT\",\n    \"ACCT-CURR-CYC-DEBIT\"\n   ],\n   \"literals\": []\n  }\n ],\n \"when\": [\n  {\n   \"text\": \"The account credit limit is less than the stored projected balance. A balance exactly equal to the limit passes.\",\n   \"fields\": [\n    \"ACCT-CREDIT-LIMIT\",\n    \"WS-TEMP-BAL\"\n   ],\n   \"literals\": []\n  }\n ],\n \"then\": [\n  {\n   \"text\": \"The failure reason is set to 102 and the description to 'OVERLIMIT TRANSACTION'.\",\n   \"fields\": [\n    \"WS-VALIDATION-FAIL-REASON\",\n    \"WS-VALIDATION-FAIL-REASON-DESC\"\n   ],\n   \"literals\": [\n    \"102\",\n    \"OVERLIMIT TRANSACTION\"\n   ]\n  }\n ]\n}"
   }
